  "worked_solution": "The polar curve $r=4$ is a circle of radius $4$ centered at the origin. It crosses the negative $y$-axis at the point where $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959689/assets/0861ee15a875e00738a237d2788e26432c1c4c128ad7510a881f31aebaaff491.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(4,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).$",
